\section{Level Map}
\label{sec:iterate}

Suppose that we are given a CSS code as a cocomplex $C=(C,\delta)$ where
\begin{equation}
    C =  X \to Q \to Z
\end{equation}
and $\bar{C} =(\bar{C},\bar{\delta})$ be that with meta-checks.
This subsection then inductively constructs CSS code $\bar{\Gamma}(C)$ with additional meta-checks only in the $Z$ sector, i.e., $MZ'$.
To construct meta-checks in the $X$ sector, a \textit{dual} iteration is applied via $\bar{\Gamma}_*(C)\equiv \bar{\Gamma}(C^\top)^\top$ so that the level map is given by the composition $\bar{\Theta} = \bar{\Gamma}_*\circ \bar{\Gamma}$ as in Lemma \ref{lem:level-map-composition}.
The following are some assumptions made to simplify the (already tedious) notation, though we remark that they can be removed and dealt with in full generality \cite{balasubramanian2026passive}.

\begin{hypothesis}[Edge-like $x,z$ Pair]
    \label{hyp:edge-like-supp}
    In general, the common support $x\wedge z$ has even cardinality if $x\prec z$. For (notation) simplicity, we shall assume that $|x\wedge z|=2$ whenever $x\prec z$ in $C$.
    Note that the assumption is self-dual, i.e., if $C$ satisfies this property, then so does it transpose $C^\top$.
\end{hypothesis}

\begin{hypothesis}[Connectivity]
    \label{hyp:connected-local-graph}
    Assume that the local graph $G^x$ as in Definition \ref{def:local-cone-x} is connected for all $x$-checks in $C$.
    Note that this assumption is not self-dual, and thus we shall also assume that the transpose $C^\top$ also satisfies, i.e., the local graphs of $z$-checks consisting of vertices $\{\prec z\}$ is connected for all $z$ checks
\end{hypothesis}

In particular, we shall show in Lemma \ref{lem:edge-like-support}-\ref{lem:connected-local-graph} that Hypotheses \ref{hyp:edge-like-supp}-\ref{hyp:connected-local-graph} hold inductively, i.e., $\Gamma(C),\Gamma_*(C)$ satisfy the hypotheses if $C$ satisfies them, so that it's sufficient to assume that only the seed code $C\super{0}$ satisfies the hypotheses.

